WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.046
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.725
Give me one minute and I'll show you

00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:11.687
how Dataflow can help you process
and enrich data at scale.

00:00:11.687 --> 00:00:14.724
Data is generated in real time
from different sources

00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:18.058
but capturing, processing,
and analyzing it is not easy

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:20.445
because it's usually not
in the desired format

00:00:20.445 --> 00:00:22.022
for your downstream systems.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.954
Solution? Dataflow.

00:00:23.954 --> 00:00:26.390
Dataflow is a serverless,
fast, and cost-effective

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.369
data-processing service
for stream and batch data

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:31.907
which removes operational
overhead by automating

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:36.081
the infrastructure provisioning,
and auto-scaling as your data grows.

00:00:36.081 --> 00:00:37.718
Using Dataflow is easy.

00:00:37.718 --> 00:00:39.541
You read the data from the source,

00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:42.064
transform it, and write it
back into a sink.

00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:45.320
It provides portability with
the processing pipeline created

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.910
using open source Apache Beam libraries

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.500
in the language of your choice
and applying it as Dataflow job

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.332
which then executes the processing
on worker virtual machines.

00:00:55.332 --> 00:00:59.321
You can create and run Dataflow jobs
using the Cloud Console UI,

00:00:59.321 --> 00:01:01.622
gCloud CLI, or the APIs.

00:01:01.622 --> 00:01:03.966
You can use prebuilt or custom templates,

00:01:03.966 --> 00:01:06.854
or write SQL statements
to develop pipelines

00:01:06.854 --> 00:01:10.716
right from BigQuery UI
or use AI Platform Notebooks.

00:01:10.716 --> 00:01:13.756
Security is taken care of
with all the data encrypted

00:01:13.756 --> 00:01:16.564
at rest and in transit
with an option to use

00:01:16.564 --> 00:01:18.447
customer-managed encryption keys.

00:01:18.447 --> 00:01:22.132
Additionally you can use private IPs
and VPC service controls

00:01:22.132 --> 00:01:23.758
to secure the environment.

00:01:23.976 --> 00:01:26.471
For all these reasons
Dataflow is a great choice

00:01:26.471 --> 00:01:28.853
for use cases such as real-time AI,

00:01:28.853 --> 00:01:31.149
data warehousing or stream analytics.

00:01:31.485 --> 00:01:34.552
So, next time you're looking
to processing and enrich any data,

00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:36.207
take a minute to look at Dataflow.

00:01:36.582 --> 00:01:40.235
To learn more, check out:
<i>cloud.google.com/Dataflow</i>

